            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0451" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/145: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Irkutsk</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Harris</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">temporarily at Harbin, to the
                            Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-04T16:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1919, 4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 12, 5:03
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>217. I understand that the Omsk Government desires 150,000 rifles ordered in
                    America should be sent to Russians for new recruits. I understand General Graves is favorably considering this
                    matter, and I recommend that it be done. Believe it would be good policy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Harris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
